abstract: >-
  GAPS is an educational resource designed to support
  researchers in the preparation, documentation, evaluation,
  and sharing of research artifacts, particularly in Empirical
  Software Engineering.


  The guidance provided in this document is not intended to
  be an exhaustive set of features for research artifacts.
  Instead, it offers examples and practical recommendations
  based on insights gathered from survey responses, the
  literature, and existing guidelines, including materials
  recommended by survey participants.


  Overall, GAPS serves as a practical tool to help
  researchers identify and prioritize key aspects when
  preparing research artifacts.
